Extracted from the full Gemini API documentation (single file, 335,605 lines, 8.9 MB) downloaded 2026-11-06 from https://aistudio.google.com/llms-full.txt and saved in Dropbox at `/gemini-api-docs-full.txt`. Local copies: `~/workspace/gemini-api-docs-full.txt` (full) and `~/workspace/gemini-api-docs-index.txt` (417-line index of every page). Model names, endpoints, and defaults below are as stated in that download — check the live docs before building on a preview model.

## The rules (from the docs themselves)
- **Canonical SDK:** `google-genai` — `pip install google-genai` or `npm install @google/genai`. Never use deprecated `google-generativeai` or `@google/generative-ai`.
- **Default API:** the **Interactions API** (`client.interactions`). `generateContent` still works but is legacy. Pages labeled `(generateContent)` cover legacy; `(v1)` is the stable v1 reference; unlabeled pages cover Interactions + v1beta.
- Every docs page is available as clean markdown by appending `.md` to its URL.
- OpenAI-compatible endpoints exist (`/v1beta/openai/chat/completions`) — standard OpenAI SDKs can call Gemini models.

## Quick start
```bash
export GEMINI_API_KEY=<redacted>
pip install -U google-genai        # Python
npm install @google/genai          # JavaScript
```
```python
from google import genai
client = genai.Client()
interaction = client.interactions.create(
    model="gemini-3.8-flash",
    input="Explain how AI works in a few words")
print(interaction.output_text)
```
```javascript
import { GoogleGenAI } from "@google/genai";
const ai = new GoogleGenAI({});
const interaction = await ai.interactions.create({
  model: "gemini-3.8-flash",
  input: "Explain how AI works in a few words",
});
console.log(interaction.output_text);
```
- Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (AI Studio creates a project + key). Paid tier = set up Cloud Billing, prepay minimum $5; higher rate limits. Usage at AI Studio Dashboard > Usage.

## REST surface
- Base: `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com` — `/v1beta` (Interactions API) and `/v1` (stable).
- Auth: API key (`?key=` or `x-goog-api-key` header); OAuth / credentials for managed agents.
- Resources: `interactions` (default call), `models` (`:generateContent`, `:streamGenerateContent`, `:embedContent`), `files`, `cachedContents`, `fileSearchStores` (RAG), `agents`, `environments`, `credentials`, `auth_tokens`, `triggers`, `webhooks`, `voices`.

